{{- $sdkName := (sanitizeClassName .Global.AST.MainSDK.Type.Name) -}}
You can setup your SDK to emit debug logs for SDK requests and responses.

You can pass a logger that matches `console`'s interface as an SDK option.

> [!WARNING]
> Beware that debug logging will reveal secrets, like API tokens in headers, in log messages printed to a console or files. It's recommended to use this feature only during local development and not in production.

```typescript
import { {{$sdkName}} } from "{{.Global.Config.PackageName}}";

const sdk = new {{$sdkName}}({ {{constants.debugLogger}}: console });
```
{{- if .Global.Config.EnvVarPrefix }}

You can also enable a default debug logger by setting an environment variable `{{ templateDebugEnvVar }}` to true.
{{- end }}